Add PEP 561 `py.typed` marker so mypy consumes VUnit's type hints.

VUnit ships partial type annotations (e.g. `Optional[str]` on public
API methods like `Library.add_source_file`) but no `py.typed` marker,
so mypy treats every `from vunit import ...` as `import-untyped` and
refuses to check consumer code that touches the VUnit API. Adding
this empty marker file opts into PEP 561 discovery — mypy honours
the shipped hints and treats absent hints as implicit `Any`, which
matches how downstream projects already interact with VUnit.

Drop this patch when VUnit upstream ships `py.typed` themselves.

